<%# NO .page wrapper of its own, deliberately. halt_if_withdrawn renders this
    under the APPLICATION layout, which has already opened <div class="page">
    -- and .page carries min-height: 100svh, so a second one nested inside it
    is a full viewport tall stacked below the sticky topbar: measured at
    390x680, 375x553 and 1280x800, the document came out 849/722/917px tall
    against content ending at y=221/220/182 -- 169/169/117px of scroll into
    nothing. Without the wrapper the document is exactly one viewport at all
    three sizes. The class was copied from the in_game layout's shell,
    which this page replaces rather than uses. Neither suite can see it --
    Capybara parses no CSS -- and bin/measure-play-screen measures the play
    screen, not this one. %>
<h2><%= t("game_passings.withdrawn.title") %></h2>

<p class="withdrawn-category">
  <%= t("games.withdrawal.categories.#{@game.withdrawal_category}") %>
</p>

<%# Operator-authored free text: verbatim, never through t(), and rendered as
    its OWN element rather than composed into a sentence -- which is what
    keeps a Turkish or Georgian case suffix off an interpolated value. %>
<% if @game.withdrawal_note.present? %>
  <p class="withdrawn-note"><%= @game.withdrawal_note %></p>
<% end %>
